From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc64: give /openprom the aligned-allocator property

OBP has an empty "aligned-allocator" property in /openprom, and the
sparc32 tree has it too. The Solaris 2.5.1 boot program (ufsboot) on
sun4u looks for it before it honours the kernel's page size hint:
without it the kernel's text and data are claimed and mapped only as
large as the segments, not as whole 4 MB pages. The kernel then puts
its nucleus hme blocks in the rest of its 4 MB data page, and its first
access there (sfmmu_add_nucleus_hblks) is a data access fault
("Unhandled Exception 0x30") before the banner. The boot program of
2.6 and later always aligns on sun4u and isn't affected.
---
 arch/sparc64/tree.fs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc64/tree.fs b/arch/sparc64/tree.fs
index fc653ac..814de6c 100644
--- a/arch/sparc64/tree.fs
+++ b/arch/sparc64/tree.fs
@@ -100,3 +100,6 @@ finish-device
 
 " /openprom" find-device
   " OBP 3.10.24 1999/01/01 01:01" encode-string " version" property
+  \ OBP has it: the Solaris 2.5.1 boot program loads the kernel's text and
+  \ data as whole 4 MB pages (its pagesize hint) only when it is there
+  0 0 " aligned-allocator" property
